---
import { Image, getImage } from 'astro:assets'
import { doc, ideCapture } from '../lib/content'
const optimized = await getImage({ src: ideCapture, width: 1800, format: 'webp', quality: 90 })
const variants = [
  { id: 'ide', name: 'Your IDE', index: '01', detail: 'Files left. Conversation right.' },
  {
    id: 'claude',
    name: 'Claude Desktop–like',
    index: '02',
    detail: 'Conversation first. Work beside it.',
  },
  {
    id: 'codex',
    name: 'Codex app–like',
    index: '03',
    detail: 'Project in view. A focused workspace.',
  },
]
---

<section id="surface" class="section surface-section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">01 / IDE view</p><h2>Keep the session.<br />Change the surface.</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="section-intro">
        Maybe you want Claude Desktop’s conversation-first shape. Maybe the Codex app’s task-focused
        feel. Or an editor beside the agent. The layout is a choice, not the engine.
      </p>
    </div>
    <fieldset class="surface-lab">
      <legend class="sr-only">Choose a layout study for the same Phosphor session</legend>
      {
        variants.map(({ id, name }) => (
          <input
            class="sr-only layout-radio"
            type="radio"
            name="surface"
            id={`layout-${id}`}
            value={id}
            checked={id === 'ide'}
            aria-label={name}
            aria-controls={`view-${id}`}
          />
        ))
      }
      <div class="surface-controls">
        <div class="surface-tabs">
          {
            variants.map(({ id, name, index }) => (
              <label for={`layout-${id}`}>
                <span>{index}</span>
                {name}
              </label>
            ))
          }
        </div>
        <span class="surface-hint">Same session / 3 arrangements</span>
      </div>
      <div class="surface-stage">
        <div id="view-ide" class="surface-view view-ide">
          <div class="view-caption">
            <span class="status-dot"></span><span>Phosphor / actual capture</span><span
              >Explorer + Monaco ↔ transcript</span
            >
          </div>
          <a
            href={ideCapture.src}
            target="_blank"
            rel="noopener"
            class="ide-original"
            aria-label="Open the full IDE capture"
          >
            <Image
              src={ideCapture}
              alt="The real Headroom Optimization session: file explorer and Monaco with TopBar.tsx docked left; Claude Opus 5 transcript and results table right; composer showing pi-claude-cli, Max thinking and 35% context usage."
              widths={[800, 1200, 1800, 2400, 3600]}
              sizes="(max-width: 700px) 94vw, 92vw"
              format="webp"
              quality={90}
              loading="eager"
            />
          </a>
        </div>
        {
          variants
            .filter(({ id }) => id !== 'ide')
            .map(({ id, name, detail }) => (
              <div id={`view-${id}`} class:list={['surface-view', `view-${id}`]}>
                <div class="view-caption">
                  <>
                    <span class="study-dot" />
                    <span>{name} / layout study</span>
                    <span>{detail}</span>
                  </>
                </div>
                <div
                  class:list={['replica', `replica-${id}`]}
                  style={`--capture: url('${optimized.src}'); --source-ratio: ${ideCapture.width / ideCapture.height}`}
                >
                  <div class="replica-nav" aria-label="Explorer crop">
                    <>
                      <span class="region-label">Explorer</span>
                      <div
                        class="crop crop-explorer"
                        role="img"
                        aria-label="The same file explorer, cropped from the real capture"
                      />
                    </>
                  </div>
                  <div class="replica-chat" aria-label="Transcript crop">
                    <>
                      <span class="region-label">Same transcript + composer</span>
                      <div
                        class="crop crop-chat"
                        role="img"
                        aria-label="The unchanged conversation and composer, cropped from the real capture"
                      />
                    </>
                  </div>
                  <div class="replica-files" aria-label="Editor crop">
                    <>
                      <span class="region-label">Same Monaco editor</span>
                      <div
                        class="crop crop-files"
                        role="img"
                        aria-label="The same TopBar.tsx editor, cropped from the real capture"
                      />
                    </>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </div>
            ))
        }
      </div>
      <div class="invariant-strip">
        <span class="mono">UNCHANGED</span><strong>pi’s agent loop</strong><span>+</span><strong
          >your extensions</strong
        ><span class="invariant-tail">Layout moves. Work stays.</span>
      </div>
    </fieldset>
    <div class="surface-notes">
      <p>
        <strong>These are arrangements, not integrations.</strong> The two app-inspired views rearrange
        crops of this same capture. They are not screenshots of Claude Desktop or Codex, and not named
        presets in Phosphor.
      </p>
      <p>
        Today you can dock one pane on either side, resize it or go fullscreen. The choice is saved
        per session. <a class="text-link" href={doc('ui-shell.md#pane-system')}>How panes work ↗</a>
      </p>
    </div>
    <p class="capture-provenance">
      Headroom Optimization · Claude Opus 5 via pi-claude-cli · Max thinking · 35% context at
      capture. <a class="text-link" href={ideCapture.src} target="_blank" rel="noopener"
        >Open the full IDE capture ↗</a>
    </p>
    <div class="numbered-notes">
      <article>
        <span>01</span><h3>The project is right there.</h3><p>
          Browse the workspace and edit in Monaco without leaving the conversation.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span><h3>The reply has structure.</h3><p>
          Text, tables and tool activity belong in a readable transcript, not a terminal dump.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span><h3>The controls stay close.</h3><p>
          Model, supported thinking level and context usage live beside the prompt.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
